Hello everyone,

We are happy to announce Early Access version 0.8 of Ezaron Defense is here. Again, based on your feedback and on our roadmap we added new features, made some changes, and also fix some bugs. A detailed list of the changes can be found down here.

This version of the game comes with a significant change: the difficulty. We read your reviews and listen to the feedback so, we decided to make the game a little harder. This update has 3 new levels: 11, 12 and 13, but these levels are more challenging than the others you already played.

These changes are not final, and we already work on a Difficulty Slider feature we want to implement, later in the game. So, for those who still think the game is too easy or too hard, have patience, new things are coming along.

note: We advise you to start a new game to have a full experience, but you can also continue playing the game from where you are right now.

Changelog:

- Two new enemy types: Melee Resistance and Magic Resistance enemy
Last update we added armored enemies. Now, some of them will also have an additional resistance layer.
Magical Resistance creatures receive less damage from Magic and Lighting towers;
Melee Resistance creatures receives less damage from Archer and Cannon towers;
Each of them has their respective aura.

- Infobox when a new enemy appears
Now, for every new creature you met, the player can choose to read some additional info. This is only the first step in our objective to create a 'Monsterpedia'

- New Level 4 Towers
Speaking of towers. 2 new tower updates are now available in-game.
Balista Tower, which has a low fire rate, but does high splash damage;
Rocket Launcher Tower, which has a very high fire rate but only target one enemy;
Don't forget that Level 4 towers are using crystals to upgrade. Crystals are earned by killing Armored creatures.

- Fixing Town Level bug
When loading a previously saved game, the town level was not correctly calculated and this may lock some of the levels;

- Fire Archer tower does more damage
It's now the strongest archer tower.

- New music track for the levels
New music added for the levels. We have 2 new tracks to listen to while fighting with the enemies.

- Overall difficulty changed
The overall game difficulty is a little higher.

Minor changes:
- Remove the reward (1 crystal) you receive when leveling up the Town Level. This does not affect the reward of crystals the player receives when making or upgrading the buildings.
- Added missing description for level 4 archer towers;
- Lich King animation fixed;
- Changed some texts;
- Polish and fixed some paths in levels;
- Some other minor visual and sound issues fixed;

Thanks to all of you for your support and the positive response! We've prepared our first patch with some bugfixes and new features; patch notes are listed below but you'll be able to see them in-game!

Patch Notes:
- Fixed a missing tower spot in level 8;
- Fixed level 3 'left' path;
- Add descriptions to magic icons when mouse over them;
- Added correct materials to NPC in town; now all npc has shadows;
- Added a Discord button in main menu;
- Fixed Minor bugs


Thank you all and see you next time!

- Raul from RVL Games
